            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Terry Wirkerman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom had a similar recipe, using 2 tbsp cornstarch. Her directions said to boil 5 minutes. After adding the butter and the vanilla, she grated in some nutmeg and a pinch of salt. When she made it, it was delicious! I have yet to make this; I'm just transcribing her recipes into my recipe software, Pepperplate. I hope it works for you!",
            "datePublished": "2024-10-05T21:18:06.712Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gary W Morris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I changed recipe ingredients to;1 cup of 2% milk, 3/4 cup of Splenda Brown Sugar Blend, 1 TSP Cinnamon, 1 Ounce of Whiskey 2 TBL Cornstarch, Bring to a Boil and Cook for 3 Minutes,",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-05T15:16:10.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SJCOLS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed several reviewers' suggestions to reduce the water to 1 cup and increase the cornstarch to 2 Tbs. I used granulated sugar. (White sugar always refers to granulated, not powdered sugar. Maybe some reviewers had trouble because they didn't blend the sugar and cornstarch completely before adding the water, or they didn't stir while it was getting hot. That would cause lumps for sure.) The consistency was perfect to go on top of Pumpkin Bread Pudding found on this site. The pudding was great and this sauce made it even better. I'm rating this 5 stars because I hate to see someone give a bad rating when the cook changed the recipe. I'm sure this is just as good as written, just a little thinner.",
            "datePublished": "2010-10-14T15:10:53.060Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tina Marie Benbow"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's funny reading the other reviews about variations, adding &amp; taking away. I followed the recipe with WHITE SUGAR &amp; it turned out AMAZING. I made it only because I didn't have CONFECTIONERS sugar for vanilla icing for my home made vanilla cake. My daughter &amp; I were delighted! I've made it twice.. Again yesterday. If you don't care for a runny sauce all you have to do is add more cornstarch. Now, I did add more butter lol. I was in the mood for something peanut buttery earlier, so I added a tablespoon of pb in a 1/2 cup of the sauce. OMG! Yummy!!! Thanks so much.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-14T15:44:50.200Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "StickySue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this sauce for Healthier Bread Pudding. I cut back on the water by half and doubled the cornstarch. I also used Splenda in place of sugar. It turn out like a sauce consistency and it tasted pretty tasty. Thanks, Happy Cooking!",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-06T11:50:12.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clydesmomma"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I followed the mods that most people mentioned, increasing to 2 T cornstarch and decreasing to 1 C water. We liked it, but I did find it a bit sweet. I will make it again, but may try it with more water to cut the sweetness. I might also try switching the vanilla extract with rum flavoring. It reminded me of butter rum sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-24T20:11:24.507Z"
          },
          {
